{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS Organizations emits CloudTrail events for account membership changes - AWS","context":"AWS Organizations now emits CloudTrail events to the management account whenever accounts join or leave the organization. These new events, AccountJoinedOrganization and AccountDepartedOrganization, provide enhanced visibility into organizational membership changes. The AccountJoinedOrganization event captures how an account joined (Created or Invited) and the join timestamp. The AccountDepartedOrganization event records how an account departed (Left for voluntary departures, Removed for account removal by the management account, or Cleaned for permanently closed accounts) and the departure timestamp. These events can be used to create CloudWatch alarms or Amazon EventBridge rules for real-time notifications, enabling rapid response to suspicious organizational changes. These CloudTrail events are available in all commercial, AWS GovCloud (US), and China Regions","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/05/aws-organizations-cloudtrail/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"setting-up-cloudtrail-multi-region","skill_description":"Enables a multi-region AWS CloudTrail trail with S3 log storage, CloudWatch Logs integration, and CloudWatch Logs Insights queries for security monitoring and compliance auditing. Use when setting up centralized API activity logging across all AWS regions.\n\nServices: cloudtrail, s3, cloudwatch, iam, kms\nTasks: configure, secure, monitor\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: security, monitoring\n*","skill_name":"setting-up-cloudtrail-multi-region"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"managing-data-asset-access","skill_description":"Grants, requests, audits and removes access to data assets in an AWS data catalog (the Amazon SageMaker Catalog supported by Amazon DataZone) through catalog subscriptions over published listings. Covers requesting a subscription, approving or rejecting requests with a recorded decision, sharing a listing with a project, revoking one or many subscriptions, and confirming grant settlement. Triggers on: give another team access to a table, request access to a dataset, approve or reject an access request, share a listing with a project, who has access to this table, revoke access, bulk revoke, is the access actually gone, subscription grant status. Not for: IAM roles, policies or STS (use aws-iam), S3 bucket policies (use securing-s3-buckets), Clean Rooms permissions (use aws-cleanrooms), or writing catalog metadata, glossaries and forms, publishing listings, or retiring or deleting an asset that other teams are subscribed to and the order of operations that needs (use managing-data-catalog)\n\n\nServices: datazone\nTasks: deploy, audit\nPersona: data-engineer, developer, architect\nWorkload: data-analytics\n*","skill_name":"managing-data-asset-access"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"amazon-ses","skill_description":"Guides Amazon SES onboarding for domain-based email sending. Covers identity configuration, production access, an optional first test send, and troubleshooting setup, authentication, or sending failures. Use when setting up SES, resuming incomplete onboarding, or leaving the sandbox. Does not cover inbound email or Mail Manager, SMS/voice, WhatsApp, SNS, Pinpoint, or WorkMail.\n\nServices: ses, route53\nTasks: onboard, configure, troubleshoot\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: email, messaging\n*","skill_name":"amazon-ses"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Verify CloudTrail get-event-selectors behavior for org trails from member accounts."}
